WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:07.789
Watching Hisoka is like watching Game of Thrones
jammed into a single character: Sex, violence,

00:00:07.789 --> 00:00:11.269
questionable moral actions, intrigue and power.

00:00:11.269 --> 00:00:17.220
He is undoubtedly one of the most iconic characters
in the history of anime, and if you have taken

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:22.420
away anything from the videos on this channel,
it's that popular characters are always successful,

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:27.840
because the author put a ton of blood, sweat
and tears into creating them. As we will see,

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.240
Hisoka is not giving you goosebumps because
he's so cool or strong or because his bungee

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:38.641
gum has the properties of gum and rubber.
Hisoka is so damn intriguing, because of all

00:00:38.641 --> 00:00:43.240
the psychology Togashi has tied up in his
personality, because of the way he uses Hisoka

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:48.560
not only as a character, but as a storytelling
device, that makes hunter x hunter what it

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:54.680
is, and because Hisoka is purposefully designed
to not only manipulate the other characters,

00:00:54.680 --> 00:01:08.170
but also to manipulate YOU dear viewer. Which
is why you love the story so much.

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:13.749
This might well be the most challenging character
analysis I have done so far. So buckle up.

00:01:13.749 --> 00:01:31.890
This is the story of Hisoka Morow.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:37.409
If I had to break it down into one sentence,
Hisoka is a manipulative, combat-addicted

00:01:37.409 --> 00:01:41.670
and powerful player in the world of hunter
x hunter, that only acts based on what gives

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:47.579
him the most pleasure. The apex of hedonism.
- That were actually two sentences - Yeah,

00:01:47.579 --> 00:01:48.880
yeah, okay, okay.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.579
Part of Hisoka's charm comes from the fact
that we know barely anything about his past.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:57.429
The only hint we ever get in the story, is
that Hisoka grew up in a state of poverty

00:01:57.429 --> 00:02:08.700
coming to cherish even the humblest of luxuries
such as a piece of bungee gum. Now, since

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:14.319
this piece of information comes from Hisoka
himself, it's even unclear whether we can

00:02:14.319 --> 00:02:20.290
trust the most manipulative person in anime
history, with being honest about his own past.

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:25.849
As we will explore in a moment however, it
is very plausible that he indeed had a quite

00:02:25.849 --> 00:02:30.519
tragic past. In this context I also want to
briefly mention the one shot about Hisoka's

00:02:30.519 --> 00:02:37.209
past made by Sui Ishida, the author of Tokyo
Goul. While not canon, it was acknowledged

00:02:37.209 --> 00:02:41.849
by Togashi, and might be worked around in
the future. In case you are not familiar with

00:02:41.849 --> 00:02:46.659
the piece, we get a short story about a heavily
injured Hisoka being taken in by a circus

00:02:46.659 --> 00:02:51.680
troupe. How did he get injured? Where did
he come from? Where was he going? We have

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:57.690
no idea. All we know, according to Hisoka,
is that his mother apparently had some proficiency

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:02.549
in illusionist arts having taught him how
to use playing cards in various ways. Working

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:07.510
with the troupe, it becomes clear that Hisoka
was an absolute prodigy, being extremely confident

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:19.440
in his own capabilities and learning new skills,
including nen at an incredible speed. He gets

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.830
involved with the murderous doings of the
troups leader, who is murdering people for

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:46.260
pleasure. Perfectly summing up Hisoka's character,
he is the one to put an end to his killing,

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:54.489
all while showing off his own cruel and pleasure
driven side. And it's quite unclear whether

00:03:54.489 --> 00:03:58.989
he does so out of a senes of morale or due
to his desire to fight and get stronger. He

00:03:58.989 --> 00:03:59.989
even forms a sort of relationship with one
of the groups members, while at the same time

00:03:59.989 --> 00:04:00.989
enjoying his own growth and dominance over
others. In the end, regardless of Hisoka's

00:04:00.989 --> 00:04:01.989
intentions or efforts he found himself with
little option but to kill, and walk away.

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:05.870
It would seem that he is destined to find
and kill strong opponents. Not only does his

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:12.319
own twisted desire compel him to seek out
such, but even if he attempts a peaceful life...the

00:04:12.319 --> 00:04:13.739
bloodshed seeks him.

00:04:13.739 --> 00:04:19.600
And I think this shows really well, that the
truth behind Hisoka's hedonism is actually

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.500
some sort of trauma he must have lived through
in his past, that turned him into the sort

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:34.130
of cold psychopath he is. And while yes, Hisoka
is a really cool character, I hope it doesn't

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:39.850
come as too big a surprise that the man has
a pretty severe personality disorder. I talk

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:45.320
about this in a bit more detail in my analysis
of Sukuna, a similar type of character, if

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:51.060
you want to learn more about the psychology
behind this. The baseline is this: Hedonism,

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:56.271
in other words, fulfilling your every desire,
is not the same thing as happiness. And by

00:04:56.271 --> 00:05:01.340
focusing solely on the present moment without
any regard for future consequences one oneself

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:06.340
and others, Hisoka completely stays clear
of his thinking back to his past. Through

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:10.900
combat, not only can he gain control about
who gets to hurt him, but he also can now

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:15.640
dominate people in return and get a sense
of importance and purpose, by delivering a

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:16.760
show for the audience.

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:22.980
That is Hisoka's true desire and drive as
a character. Satisfying his own desires, which

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:26.040
mostly is finding and fighting powerful people.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:30.770
After all, he is a true tactical genius and
phenomenal martial artist himself. However,

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:35.310
I think the best way to understand how Hisoka
ticks, is by looking at his nen abilities.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:42.850
Did you know for instance that Bungee gum
has the properties of both gum and rubber?

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:47.490
Just like killua, Hisoka also belongs to the
transmuter category, who's users are said

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:53.320
to be deceptive, fickle and driven by desire.
And I think there is probably no other character

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:59.100
that fits this description better than our
psychopathic clown. First of all deception.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:05.570
Hisoka is arguably the best liar in the series.
Not just in the art of making false, but believable

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:11.280
statements; but in crafting meticulous, intricate
webs of deception that completely obscure

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:18.110
the truth. Hisoka literally means secretive
in Japanese, so you know it's one of his most

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:24.430
defining traits. He is a maser of manipulating
people, both in and outside of combat, often

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:29.970
putting multiple layers of lies on top of
each other. Hisoka uses this to divert attention,

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:36.010
create openings, hide his own weaknesses and
sometimes simply make his opponent suffer.

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:41.590
A great example for this is of course his
battle with Kastro. He willingly sacrifices

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:48.830
his arms to create an opening, divert attention,
and pretend having supernatural powers, at

00:06:48.830 --> 00:07:02.330
the same time hiding the fact that he actually
DID injure himself, all while throwing his

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:07.400
opponent into utter madness, forcing him to
loose his cool and humiliating him in front

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:24.300
of the audience. Another example of this is
his prediction that Kastro would "die dancing".

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:28.750
Quite understandably, Kastro didn't believe
the words of a notorious liar and didn't give

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:33.110
it much thought. Meanwhile, people that have
come to know this aspect of Hisoka, such as

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:38.080
Gon and Killua may find themselves easily
trusting Hisoka's words at face value only

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:43.960
to find it was all a facade in the end. In
true Transmuter fashion only Hisoka himself

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:55.860
can ever know for certain what is truth and
what is lie.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:08:00.930
Hisoka is also extremely fickle. Often, what
used to be a year-long obsession of his, can

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:05.930
become irrelevant to him in moments, like
with our example of Kastro, or his infiltration

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:07.220
of the Phantom Troupe.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:11.470
And of course, the most defining trait of
Hisoka, his Hedonism that is driven and motivated

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:14.460
only by what makes him feel good. No matter
if it's becoming a member of the worlds most

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:20.310
dangerous criminal organization to fight their
leader or pushing two young boys to become

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:25.180
strong hunters in order to fight them in the
future, Hisoka doesn't let himself be deterred

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:30.610
from getting what he wants. Injury, failure
and even death only seem to make it all the

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:36.640
more fun for him. This hedonisms is expressed
by Hisoka in many ways, but I want to look

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:44.099
at two aspects in particular here: Sex and
violence.

00:08:44.099 --> 00:08:49.900
Let's start with the latter. Hisoka is literally
addicted to fighting. As in he can't live

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:54.210
without it. And in this context I think it's
worth talking about his relationship with

00:08:54.210 --> 00:09:08.540
the protagonist as well. Despite the differences
between Gon and Hisoka, the two find themselves

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:14.160
inextricably drawn to each other. On the surface,
both appear to be opposites, right down to

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:18.820
Hisoka’s appearance as a scary clown — the
mortal enemy of pre-pubescents everywhere

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:24.890
— but as the show continues their differences
blur into similarity.&nbsp;Both Gon and Hisoka

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:30.120
share the classic shounen trope of the warrior.
These are characters that are abnormally proficient

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:38.450
in battle, learn fast, tolerate pain and derive
a seemingly unhealthy, almost addictive level

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:43.640
of pleasure from it. Other such examples include
Kenpachi from Bleach, Sukuna from Jujutsu

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:48.600
Kaisen and of course Goku and Vegeta from
the Dragonball franchise. For these types

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:53.300
of characters there seems to be little choice.
Everything in their life seems to lead them

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:58.550
toward combat even if they try to avoid it.
In other words, this desire to better ones

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:03.530
powers and defining one's entire existence
through battle are not at all unique to&nbsp;Hunter

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:08.960
x Hunter. However, while most shonen tend
to avoid the problems associated with this

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:12.940
stance, Togashi, as he so often likes to do,
calls out this issue, by making it a central

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:18.001
part of both Gon's and Hisoka's character.
The reason they enjoy fighting is that it

00:10:18.001 --> 00:10:22.980
gives them a sense of importance, having people
notice and fear them, and gaining a sense

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:28.280
of control. They have the power to have an
impact on the world. As a great example of

00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:30.420
this, and how strong Hisoka's influence on
Gon is, let's return to the fight in the Heaven's

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:36.990
arena, where Hisoka without any need to do
so, sacrifices an arm to prove his superiority,

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:44.220
satisfy his desire to dominate his foe and
gain the upper hand. Pun ABSOLUTELY intended.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:50.170
Later, in the Greed Island arc, Gon mirrors
Hisoka’s sacrifice against the Genthru,

00:10:50.170 --> 00:11:02.250
throwing away a carefully thought out plan
to dominate his foe.

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:07.110
But as if Hisoka was not already a masterpiece
of a manga character, subverting a number

00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:12.250
of classic tropes and rules, Togashi decided
to do something even more unusual with his

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:17.190
character. Because based on his immense self-confidence
and as a way to express his hedonism, Hisoka's

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:22.650
character carries a very interesting sexual
element as well. And yes, I know it's probably

00:11:22.650 --> 00:11:27.920
a bad idea discussing this, but hey, if you
like Hisoka that's part of his character.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:32.600
That guy literally flaunts it in everyone's
face. It's like with real people, you only

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:41.010
get them as a package. - - Deal with it.
In general, in an industry that focuses heavily,

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:47.880
and often a bit too heavily on female sexuality,
Hisoka is a rare case of a male being over

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:53.220
sexualized. This is especially interesting,
as Hunter x Hunter is still considered a Shounen

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:59.150
story, a genre aimed at young boys with strong
heroes fighting against evil. SO not exactly

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:05.210
a scenario that requires a sexy, somewhat
queer man to be involved, but here we are.

00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:11.420
This part of Hisoka's character is quite open
for interpretation, and it's meant to be that

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:15.240
way by Togashi. The main point of this, however
has actually surprisingly little to do with

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:21.160
sexuality in itself. Hisoka dressing and behaving
the way he does, are a visual representation

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:27.820
of him not giving a fuck about the rules and
embracing who he is. And since he is a hedonistic

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:31.820
magician, well, that's what you get. The other
thing is that for Hisoka, the line between

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:37.990
sexuality and violence is quite fluent and
often vanishes completely. Sigmund Freud would

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:42.650
be proud of Togashi. The much debated scene
where he gets aroused by walking behind killua

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:47.710
and gon, can of course again be interpreted
in many ways, but what gets overlooked, is

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:51.761
the fact that Hisoka in this scene gets aroused
by thinking about fighting Killua and Gon

00:12:51.761 --> 00:12:57.720
once they have grown up. And while this aspect
of Hisoka might make some people uncomfortable,

00:12:57.720 --> 00:13:03.380
it is exactly that fact that makes him such
a fascinating character. Hisoka doesn't care

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:15.350
what you think. And so this refreshing role-reversal
serves as a central element underlining who

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:17.860
Hisoka is as a person.

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:20.830
Many of these central traits, that we just
talked about, can also be found in the symbolism

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:26.200
of his character, that, you might find this
either very surprising or not at all, had

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:31.750
some inspiration from the Jojo series. For
instance, A central theme for Hisoka throughout

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:37.339
the story is the number 4, like the 44 name
tag, or his number 4 within the phantom troupe.

00:13:37.339 --> 00:13:42.980
The 4 is an unlucky number in Japan. Maybe
you know that 4 is yon in Japanese. But there

00:13:42.980 --> 00:13:50.920
is a second word for 4, which is shi, which
also means death. And death truly is all around

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:56.210
Hisoka. Another theme is that of the clown,
the fool or the joker, a very common trope

00:13:56.210 --> 00:14:01.120
in storytelling. However, Hisoka is not the
the warmhearted fool, but the intelligent

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:10.420
trickster. This character is known for his
intelligence, is close to unpredictable and

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:15.710
due to their non-conformity incredibly irritating
to anyone who follows the general rules of

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:20.990
society. Next to Hisoka, another famous example
of this is of course the joker from batman,

00:14:20.990 --> 00:14:26.540
who based on these same traits has reached
a similar level of popularity. As a clown,

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:31.120
Hisoka is of course also a performer. You
only see him fighting in a serious manner,

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:36.680
when he is facing a very strong opponent,
such as chrollo. Otherwise, the focus is always

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:47.370
on delivering a show for the audience, himself
and even his opponent. Always with another

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:52.120
twist and another ace up his sleeve, guiding
the audiences from act to act. From setup

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.710
to rising action, apparent defeat and a resolution.
If you want to go really meta here, you could

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:59.570
say that Togashi has created a storyteller
in his own story.

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:03.860
But even more than that, Hisoka is much more
than a interesting character, that enhances

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:09.560
the story. He is a carefully crafted narrative
tool, that shapes the story and characters

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:14.800
around him. Thus, Hisoka is, perhaps, one
of the most sutbtle but at the same time impactful

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:20.000
examples of Togashi's writing brilliance.
By making Hisoka purely hedonistic in nature

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:25.610
with no particular goal outside of being entertained
Hisoka can easily adapt to any purpose the

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:30.060
story requires of him. He is a true wildcard,
that in the true sense of a magician, can

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:34.440
take on any number roles, be it an ally or
antagonist. He is the one that enables Gon

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:39.209
passing the hunter exam and triggering his
desire to become stronger, ultimately forcing

00:15:39.209 --> 00:15:48.610
him and killua to master nen. He is the one
that tips of Kurapika about the gathering

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:54.210
of the phantom troupe. And on greed island,
that already has a powerful antagonist, he

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:58.811
happily takes the side of the protagonists
to advance their respective interests. At

00:15:58.811 --> 00:16:03.089
the same time, right from the start, Hisoka
is also the one shown to kill without warning

00:16:03.089 --> 00:16:08.010
or hesitation, always oozing bloodlust and
as mentioned before, being fickle to the degree

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:12.130
that you can never be sure when he will stop
helping. During the chimera ant arc, where

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:16.623
the focus is on a new over-powerful antagonist
and gon and killua now have to show their

00:16:16.623 --> 00:16:17.623
development and fend for themselves, it is
in no way unnatural for Hisoka, who wouldn't

00:16:17.623 --> 00:16:18.940
fit the arc's theme, to be away somewhere,
chasing after Chrollo, only to reappear in

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:24.300
the next arc as an antagonist to Killua and
a force of nature during the Succession war

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:34.480
arc.

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:41.370
And next to his ability to seamlessly adapt
to any circumstances in the story, he also

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:46.100
is a wonderful tool to demonstrate the progression
of the story and to power-scale the other

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:49.720
characters. Due to his obsession with fighting,
we get a very good impression of how powerful

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:54.800
Hisoka is, giving us a great insight into
many of the characters he encounters. Hisoka

00:16:54.800 --> 00:17:00.810
was always meant to be extremely strong, but
not Uber-powerful, like Netero or Meruem.

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:05.499
As a wild card he can be a powerful ally or
villain, but is never meant to be the main

00:17:05.499 --> 00:17:06.959
antagonist.

00:17:06.959 --> 00:17:11.119
The reason he's so good at showing us the
progression of the story and of the characters

00:17:11.119 --> 00:17:16.270
around him, is not because of his ever-changing
wardrobe - though, let's be honest, it's always

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:21.329
Nice when anime characters bother to buy more
than one set of clothes. Not only fashion

00:17:21.329 --> 00:17:29.820
wise, but also functionality wise. Jesus.
I mean this is fashionable. Uhm where was

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:35.239
I going with this again? Oh yeah, it's not
because of fashion, but because of his flat

00:17:35.239 --> 00:17:40.919
character arc, that Hisoka makes a great mark
for character growth of Gon, Killua and co.

00:17:40.919 --> 00:17:44.230
Character arcs are always about a character
believing something about the world, that

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:49.110
is false. In a positive arc, like killua,
it's about discovering this lie and rectifying

00:17:49.110 --> 00:17:52.730
it and becoming a better person. In a negative
arc, like Gons, it's quite similar, with the

00:17:52.730 --> 00:17:57.129
difference that at the moment of revelation,
in Gon's case his meeting with Pitou, the

00:17:57.129 --> 00:18:02.659
central moral insight fails to happen, and
the character falls deeper into his lie, becoming

00:18:02.659 --> 00:18:07.820
a worse person for it. A flat character arc
therefor, belongs to a character, that already

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:12.059
knows the truth. In the case of hunter x hunter,
this truth by the way, is the fact that people

00:18:12.059 --> 00:18:17.629
usually aren't good or bad, they are grey
and morally highly complex people, driven

00:18:17.629 --> 00:18:23.220
by desires, thoughts and the people around
them. Gon fails to realize this and keeps

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:30.369
believing that everyone is either good or
bad. Killua understands this after removing

00:18:30.369 --> 00:18:38.059
illumine needle and thus finally becomes able
to love himself, despite his faults. Hisoka

00:18:38.059 --> 00:18:41.700
already knows this. He knows who he is and
what he wants. Hisoka has learned to accept

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:46.309
the good and bad in himself and not be held
back by doubt or shame. Bow obviously, only

00:18:46.309 --> 00:18:50.710
because a character understands the truth,
it doesn't mean he always does the right thing.

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:56.950
What makes flat characters interesting is
how they act based on their insight. It often

00:18:56.950 --> 00:19:01.379
makes such characters a lot more versatile
and complex, as they can use this truth to

00:19:01.379 --> 00:19:06.710
do both good and bad to the world. Thus, Hisoka
isn't just this one dimensional character

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:11.480
as some people like to believe. Which is why
I love the shower scene, which might be the

00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:25.230
single most important moment of his character.
What the narrator is basically saying here

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:30.309
is "sit back, turn your brain off, and enjoy
the shitshow that is Hisoka's life." And since

00:19:30.309 --> 00:19:34.549
Hisoka doesn't have to go through the same
process of learning the truth anymore as the

00:19:34.549 --> 00:19:40.440
other characters, we can see their development
in comparison to the constant that is Hisokas

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:41.440
character.

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:46.000
And that brings me to the main point of this
video. Based on all that we have talked about,

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:51.210
all the fantastic writing and character design,
the thing that truly makes Hisoka a masterpiece

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:56.639
of storytelling, is the fact that You, dear
viewer are being manipulated by Hisoka as

00:19:56.639 --> 00:20:05.639
well. As am I. This becomes clear in all the
controversy around him. Is he good or bad?

00:20:05.639 --> 00:20:11.910
A role model or the worst type of person?
Relatable or repulsive? All these conflicting

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:16.019
emotions are the true genius behind Togashi's
writing. We get so many mixed informations

00:20:16.019 --> 00:20:17.019
about this man, sometimes good, soemtimes
bad. Sometimes acting like a human, sometimes

00:20:17.019 --> 00:20:18.019
like a monster. Sometimes telling the truth
and sometimes lying. Never showing any doubt

00:20:18.019 --> 00:20:20.029
about himself or his beliefs. Is Hisoka actually
good at heart, but has a hard shell? Or is

00:20:20.029 --> 00:20:25.080
he actually just cruel and selfish to the
core, manipulating us, just like the other

00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:30.619
characters, into thinking he has a good side?
Or something in between? We will probably

00:20:30.619 --> 00:20:35.669
never be able to tell. We love him for his
cool manner and his fantastic fighting skills,

00:20:35.669 --> 00:20:41.330
but despise him for his cruelty and lies.
And so, all we can really do is get sweaty

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:46.820
hands whenever he shows up, not knowing if
we're gonna get the carrot or the stick. Togashi

00:20:46.820 --> 00:20:51.399
created this character to thrust the central
moral argument of hunter x hunter into our

00:20:51.399 --> 00:20:57.009
face. Human morality is complex. There is
no clear black and white. SO we might as well

